5. NemoClaw-Thor (PLE / ngram serving ideas)                      MIT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
https://github.com/pastoriomarco/NemoClaw-Thor — Copyright Marco Pastorio.
Any Mjolnir implementation of the partially-resident-embedding (PLE) n-gram
table serving from that project's recipes — the CLOCK slot pool, the disk
page-cache path, the prefetch/early-row-fetch split — is a reimplementation
and MUST carry this attribution in the patch, module docstring or config
comment that first ships it (per the repo convention: new third-party
derivation -> this file). The qwen4 gap analysis
(docs/faq/qwen4-27b.md, "The NemoClaw-Thor gap analysis") is the design
record; the upstream PLE disk offload itself is vLLM #59958, in the base
since 0.34.0. The first such implementation is src/mjolnir/mjolnir/qwen4exp/
ple_disk.py, ple_disk_table.py and ple_disk_cache.py (the slot-pool cache and
prefetch in front of that upstream disk table).

